cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Guaraci in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Guaraci: Monte Carlo radiation transport on CPU and GPU"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hauradou
    given-names: Harlley
    email: hhauradou@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3560-9708"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/HarlleyHauradou/guaraci"
url: "https://guaraci.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  Guaraci is a Monte Carlo code for radiation transport in matter, aimed first
  at medical physics and nuclear medicine. It transports photons, electrons and
  positrons, reads human-readable input files with physical units, downloads
  its nuclear data (ENDF/B-VIII.0) from the official sources, and scores dose
  maps, doses in volumes and fluence spectra with their uncertainties.
keywords:
  - Monte Carlo
  - radiation transport
  - medical physics
  - nuclear medicine
  - dosimetry
  - electron transport
  - Rust
